{
  "query": "You are the Cloud Database Engineer for AlpineCart, a nationwide grocery delivery startup, and you must design a disaster recovery plan for production systems. The platform uses a managed database service in Google Cloud and also runs latency sensitive services on an on-premises bare metal stack in a primary data center. The plan must deliver strong transactional consistency, an RPO that is very close to zero, and a fast failover so that order processing can resume quickly. Which combination of Google Cloud solutions should you implement to meet these goals?",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Cloud Spanner with a multi-region configuration and Google Anthos Bare Metal for replicating the on-premises estate",
      "explanation": "This pairs a globally distributed relational database with an on-premises Kubernetes platform that runs on customer hardware to manage containerized workloads.",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "AlloyDB for PostgreSQL with cross-region read replicas and Cloud VMware Engine to mirror the bare metal apps",
      "explanation": "This combines a high performance PostgreSQL compatible service that supports read replicas across regions with a managed VMware platform hosted in Google Cloud for running virtual machines.",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Cloud Spanner in a multi-region topology together with Google Bare Metal Solution to mirror the on-premises environment",
      "explanation": "This uses a strongly consistent globally distributed relational database and a hosted bare metal footprint in Google Cloud that can recreate the physical environment for rapid recovery.",
      "correct": true,
      "selected": false
    },
